            "n_events": 27,
            "result_text": "Done! The function uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to enforce the concurrency limit and handles keyboard interrupts gracefully:\n\n- **Concurrency control**: The semaphore ensures only `max_concurrent` tasks run simultaneously\n- **Cleanup on interrupt**: When KeyboardInterrupt is raised, instead of immediately exiting, the function waits for all running tasks to complete with `return_exceptions=True`, allowing their finally blocks and cleanup code to execute before re-raising the interrupt\n\nYou can import and use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def some_task():\n    try:\n        # task work\n        pass\n    finally:\n        # cleanup code runs even on Ctrl+C\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([some_task, another_task, ...], max_concurrent=5)\n```"
